==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|baseball}} A ball that has been hit by a [[batter]] who started to run towards first base while holding the bat back over the plate, typically in an attempt to get a [[hit]] rather than to [[sacrifice]]
#: ''Jones fielded the '''drag bunt''', but the runner beat out his throw for a [[single]].''
# {{lb|en|baseball}} The act of bunting while running towards first base
#: {{ux|en|The '''drag bunt''' is a skill that few players perfect.}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|baseball|transitive}} to [[bunt]] while running towards [[first base]]
#: {{ux|en|Jones '''drag bunted''' the pitch.}}
# {{lb|en|baseball|intransitive}} to [[bunt]] while running towards [[first base]]
#: {{ux|en|Smith often '''drag bunts''' if he sees the third baseman playing back.}}